                    {
                        "sense_id": "e3015633-187c-3b52-9dd1-d1d2b7e7adc6",
                        "entry_id": "534e70f8-8153-31ef-887b-1aa91965112e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "boredom, ennui (state of being bored)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f80574d8-f7ff-4ddb-81b9-7d9c7fb36e40",
                                "sense_id": "e3015633-187c-3b52-9dd1-d1d2b7e7adc6",
                                "text": "Жизнь в его́ глаза́х разделя́лась на две полови́ны: одна́ состоя́ла из труда́ и ску́ки — э́то у него́ бы́ли сино́нимы; друга́я — из поко́я и ми́рного весе́лья.",
                                "translation": "Life, in his eyes, divided up into two halves: one consisted of work and tedium, which to him were synonyms; the other of tranquility and peaceful merriment.",
                                "english": "Life, in his eyes, divided up into two halves: one consisted of work and tedium, which to him were synonyms; the other of tranquility and peaceful merriment."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
